{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>דברתי.</b> Because the heart is the dwelling-place of the spirit and it is created first in the body, for it is the likeness of a king and the brain is the commander of the army, the heart was a term of designation for wisdom and understanding and reason and the thoughts of discernment, because it is the first vehicle for the supernal soul of man. And likewise words are designated by 'lip,' because words go out from it. And therefore it says: 'A wise and understanding heart' (1 Kings 3:12); 'short of heart' (Proverbs 10:13); 'he who loves his soul' (Proverbs 11:17). And the meaning of 'I grew great and increased wisdom' is that he composed and taught the wisdom of the ancients and added to theirs." "<b>ולבי ראה הרבה חכמה.</b> That he did not compose it. And the word הרבה is found with singular and plural, as in 'כי הרבה יהיו' (Isaiah 9:6). And likewise the word ריקם; and the passive participle with kamatz gadol: 'הרבה ארבה' (Genesis 16:10)."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:08.655414044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}